This project presents a Sales Forecasting System that uses both classical and deep learning approaches to predict future sales trends based on historical transaction data. 

The dataset, consisting of daily sales from April 2019, was cleaned, aggregated, and analyzed to visualize patterns and seasonality. 

An ARIMA model was implemented to generate a 7-day sales forecast, providing a statistically grounded baseline. 

To complement this, an LSTM (Long Short-Term Memory) neural network was trained on scaled time-series data using a sliding window approach, offering a more flexible and adaptive forecasting method. 

Both models were evaluated using MAPE and RMSE metrics to assess their accuracy. 

This dual-model approach highlights the practical application of machine learning and time-series analysis in inventory and revenue planning for businesses.

